{
  "id": 114904180,
  "iid": 4071,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "RTCP: Fix padding dissection in transport feedback (#15892)",
  "description": "The transport feedback definition, from (https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-holmer-rmcat-transport-wide-cc-extensions-01#section-3.1) has the third bit as the padding bit (as any RTCP feedback message). However, the transport feedback dissector was consuming the padding (if present), leaving the outer RTCP dissector with a padding bit set, but no padding to analyze/show. That resulted in a \"Malformed packet\" error.\n\nWith this patch, any padding that is consumed in the transport feedback dissection clears the outer padding bit set, leaving the RTCP dissector happy.\n\nFixes #15892",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-09-01T13:31:39.088Z",
